        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The change has been submitted. Summary of what was done:\n\n1. **`src/blinker/base.py`** — Added an `isinstance(name, str)` check at the top of `Namespace.signal` that raises `TypeError` before any dictionary lookup or modification, so non-string names are rejected even if the namespace already contains that key. `str` subclasses and the empty string are accepted (both satisfy `isinstance(name, str)`). Because the module-level `signal` helper is the bound method `default_namespace.signal`, it inherits the same validation. Signal identity for repeated names, docstring handling, independent names, and receiver dispatch are untouched.\n\n2. **`CHANGES.rst`** — Added a changelog entry under the unreleased 1.10.0 section, and a `.. versionchanged:: 1.10` note in the method docstring.",
